{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790254842,"nonce":"xvcBhBMknPt7lsp1b64cFJ1Dt78=","title":"Inliner: a callee with calls is capped at 48 instructions, cold error arms included","message":"classify() sets has_calls for any call by id, including calls to cold functions (zl_type_error, zl_annotate, zl_index_nil), and then refuses a callee over MAX_INLINE_INSTS_WITH_CALLS = 48 instructions. is_real_call already treats a cold callee as no call for the hot-site and dispatch tests; classify does not.\n\nCase: op_overload's __add handler (lua$anon$1). After the field-read change in package l2 its HIR is 71 instructions in 14 blocks, one real call (zl_arr_shared) and two cold raise arms, yet it is still TooLarge and every a + b in the loop stays a call. The six slot reads alone (ptrtoint, inttoptr, gep, bitcast, load each) are 30 instructions, so a handler that allocates cannot get under 48 however small its error paths are.\n\nOptions: count only real calls (is_real_call) for has_calls in classify, and/or exclude instructions in blocks_leading_to_cold from total_insts when weighing a callee.","files":null}]}